  "body": "The maintainer set the scope of #917 on 2026-11-20: part 3 (#2790) removes `truck-stepio`, `ruststep` and `truck-topology`. The other truck crates stay for the kernel that does not read STEP. This issue holds that work.\n\n## Now\n\nAfter #2790, these stay in the workspace:\n\n- `TruckKernel` in `crates/kernel` (`truck_impl.rs`, behind the `truck` feature).\n- Its tests: `agreement.rs`, `blend.rs`, `heal_import.rs`.\n- The truck crates that it needs (`truck-modeling`, `truck-shapeops`, `truck-meshalgo` and the crates that they pull in). About nine `truck-*` packages stay in `Cargo.lock`.\n\n## Wanted\n\n- Decide what replaces each use of `TruckKernel`: the solidcore kernel, recorded readings, or a removal.\n- Remove the `truck` feature, `truck_impl.rs` and each `truck-*` entry from each `Cargo.toml` and from `Cargo.lock`.\n- Remove the truck notices from `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` and `site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt` when no truck code stays.\n- The `#[test]` count does not go down without a named reason.\n\n## Design first\n\nThis is `P8`: the comparison tests need a decision before code. The first \"Done means\" item of #917 (no `truck-*` package in `Cargo.lock`) is met by this issue, not by #917.\n\nPart of #27. Refs #917, #2790.\n",
